cription":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":889,"end":889,"description":"Phosphoserine; by PKC"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":890,"end":890,"description":"Phosphoserine; by PKC"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":896,"end":896,"description":"Phosphoserine; by PKC"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":897,"end":897,"description":"Phosphoserine; by PKC"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Heterotetramer; the NMDAR subunits are modular and harbor tiered domains that function in concert to regulate opening and closing of the cation-selective ion channel pore (PubMed:36309015, PubMed:38598639). Forms heterotetrameric channels composed of two GluN1/zeta subunits (GRIN1), and two identical GluN2/epsilon subunits (GRIN2A, GRIN2B, GRIN2C or GRIN2D) or GluN3 subunits (GRIN3A or GRIN3B) (in vitro) (PubMed:26875626, PubMed:26919761, PubMed:28105280, PubMed:28126851, PubMed:34186027, PubMed:36309015, PubMed:36959261, PubMed:7685113). Can also form heterotetrameric channels that contain at least two GluN1 subunits and at least two different GluN2 subunits (or a combination of one GluN2 and one GluN3 subunits) (in vitro) (PubMed:36309015). In vivo, the subunit composition may vary in function of the expression levels of the different subunits (By similarity). Found in a complex with GRIN2A or GRIN2B, GRIN3A and PPP2CB (By similarity). Found in a complex with GRIN2A or GRIN2B and GRIN3B (By similarity). Interacts with SNX27 (via PDZ domain); the interaction is required for recycling to the plasma membrane when endocytosed and prevent degradation in lysosomes (By similarity). Interacts with DLG4 and MPDZ. Interacts with LRFN1 and LRFN2 (By similarity). Interacts with MYZAP (PubMed:18849881). Found in a complex with DLG4 and PRR7 (By similarity). Found in a complex with GRIN2B and PRR7 (PubMed:27458189). Interacts with PRR7; the interaction is reduced following NMDA receptor activity (PubMed:27458189)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q05586-2","name":"1","synonyms":["Short","NR1-1"],"notes":[],"length":885,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000371559.8"],"refseq":["NM_000832.7"],"refseqProteins":["NP_000823.4"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,863]],"edits":[{"start":864,"end":938,"original":"DRKSGRAEPDPKKKATFRAITSTLASSFKRRRSSKDTSTG","replacement":"QYHPTDITGPLNLSDPSVSTVV","added":22}],"missing":75,"replaced":0,"novel":22,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[31,75,0],[33,1,0],[34,1,0],[35,1,0],[36,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q05586-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q05586-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":85.9,"plddt":[[0,1],[50,13],[0,1],[50,2],[0,4],[50,2],[70,3],[90,7],[70,1],[90,16],[70,3],[50,3],[70,3],[90,7],[70,6],[90,21],[70,4],[50,4],[70,3],[90,17],[70,2],[90,31],[70,8],[90,20],[70,5],[50,4],[70,2],[90,8],[70,1],[90,7],[70,1],[90,2],[70,4],[90,25],[70,1],[90,1],[70,1],[90,10],[70,3],[90,15],[70,3],[90,16],[70,12],[90,2],[70,8],[90,14],[70,6],[90,2],[70,1],[90,11],[70,1],[90,9],[70,2],[90,8],[70,4],[90,2],[70,5],[90,4],[70,14],[90,19],[70,3],[90,6],[70,5],[90,8],[70,3],[50,8],[70,3],[90,28],[70,4],[90,1],[70,1],[90,1],[70,11],[90,9],[70,3],[90,34],[70,3],[50,3],[70,1],[50,1],[70,6],[90,2],[70,1],[90,16],[70,8],[50,4],[0,9],[50,4],[70,6],[90,1],[70,1],[90,8],[70,3],[50,1],[70,6],[90,1],[70,2],[90,20],[70,7],[50,3],[70,1],[50,1],[70,4],[90,4],[70,1],[90,4],[70,2],[90,8],[70,1],[90,25],[70,2],[90,27],[70,5],[90,4],[70,1],[90,13],[70,4],[90,25],[70,7],[50,10],[70,9],[90,20],[70,23],[50,4],[0,20]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"Q05586-3","name":"2","synonyms":["Medium","NR1-2"],"notes":[],"length":901,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000371550.8"],"refseq":["NM_021569.4"],"refseqProteins":["NP_067544.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,863],[864,901,38]],"edits":[{"start":864,"end":900,"original":"DRKSGRAEPDPKKKATFRAITSTLASSFKRRRSSKDT","